    "extract": "Punctaconchus is a genus of microconchid tubeworms. It was the last genus of microconchids, and the only genus to exist beyond the Triassic. Their tubes have large pores (punctae) penetrating the tube wall. Tubes lumen is covered by\nripplemark−like transverse ridges. Punctaconchus occurs in the Middle Jurassic of England, France and Poland.",
    "extract_html": "<p><i><b>Punctaconchus</b></i> is a genus of microconchid tubeworms. It was the last genus of microconchids, and the only genus to exist beyond the Triassic. Their tubes have large pores (punctae) penetrating the tube wall. Tubes lumen is covered by\nripplemark−like transverse ridges. <i>Punctaconchus</i> occurs in the Middle Jurassic of England, France and Poland.</p>"
